    0.2
   ],
   "edge_clearance": 0.4,
   "hole_to_hole": 0.5,
   "min_through_hole": 0.2,
   "min_track": 0.1,
   "why": "LQFP-100 at 0.5 mm pitch on a 40 mm board; JLC's multilayer line is 0.09 / 0.09 mm, 0.15 mm drill"
  },
  "planes": {
   "In1.Cu": "GND",
   "In3.Cu": "5V"
  },
  "pours": {
   "In2.Cu": "3V3"
  },
  "notes": "6 layers: F signals / In1 GND plane / In2 signals, then 3V3 poured after routing / In3 5V plane / In4 signals, then GND poured / B signals. 5V is a plane because it reaches both LDOs, three ports, the pads and the USB diode across the whole board: as 0.5 mm tracks it was left open in Freerouting's solves (2026-10-05), as was the gyro cluster on 4 layers. The IMUs sit under the MCU at the board's centre, away from the BECs on the left."
 },
